    "comment": "A brush's smudge mixes the paint it carries in the brush's own blend mode. A 1536 by 512 document holds two panels side by side, each a saturated blue chunk beside a saturated yellow one, the left at x 0 to 512 and the right at x 1024 to 1536, with the chunk between left as the grey ground. Oil Smudge at a radius of 40 pixels in the blue itself, its colour rate off so what it lays past the seam is its carry alone, its pickup at 0.15 so the blue lasts into the yellow and its flow at 1, drags the blue over the seam into the yellow three times in each panel, at y 140, 256 and 372: in Normal on the left and in the mixing mode on the right. Normal's smear goes grey in the yellow, Pigment's goes green."
